WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.390
Fushiguro isn't sasuke.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:09.290
Okay, with that out of the way, Quick question
for you: what exactly happened between this

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:18.029
scene here, at the beginning of the story
- and this scene here at the end of the anime's

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:24.640
first season? - the two sequences mirror each
other pretty closely.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.470
Both times the three first years are sent
to investigate a seemingly average case without

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.330
the support of any other jujutsu sorcerer,
both times nobora gets taken from the room

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.800
and both times it turns out that the curse
they are facing is actually a special grade

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.480
that has consumed one of sukunas fingers.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.770
And yet everything is different.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:50.710
first of all all three of them, voluntarily
enter the curses domain instead of suddenly

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.410
being trapped in it.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:01:02.210
This time it is Itadori that goes after nobora,
both of them have grown stronger and together

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:12.200
they take out the two special grades in a
very impressive manner.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.400
These two missions are clearly set up to show
the growth of our protagonists here.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.500
And while especially itadoris difference in
power and mentality is clearly visible, the

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.390
most drastic character development in this
scene is without any doubt that of Fushiguro,

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:27.180
who doesn't run away like last time, but stands
his ground, lets loose and ultimately defeats

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:32.100
the very same special grade that had seemed
unbeatable just a few weeks earlier, all with

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.299
a maniac grin on his face.

00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:36.119
So, what happened here?

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:38.149
Who is Megumi?

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:43.220
Why does his role as the typical rival slash
deuteragonist to Itadori work so much better

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.229
than in many other stories?

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:49.719
And why is he so important to both sukuna
and gojo?

00:01:49.719 --> 00:02:07.490
This is the story of Megumi Fushiguro.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.270
On the surface, Fushiguro seems to be your
typical rival character.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:17.459
While Itadori appears to have a light mood,
is extremely extroverted and runs mostly on

00:02:17.459 --> 00:02:29.420
emotions and instinct, Megumi seems to be
the classic contrast to that.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.459
With dark spiky hair, a quiet and calculating
personality, and having gown up an orphan

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:35.280
due to the harsh clan system of the jujutsu
world, he seems to be the classic trope of

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.500
the cool and brooding rival.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.489
the introversion to itadoris extroversion.

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:42.310
The dark to itadoris light.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.989
Fushigoru isn't sasuke.

00:02:43.989 --> 00:02:49.090
Because, just as Itadori subverts trope after
trope of your typical shouen protagonist,

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:51.980
fushiguro is nothing like sasuke or bakugo.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:57.100
His character actually comes a lot closer
to some of Togashi's characters like Kurapika

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:10.219
or Hiei from YuYu Hakusho.

00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:15.829
But as always, Akutami has taken a number
of successful character tropes, merged them

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:21.350
and made a character that is much more complex
and intriguing than the sum of its parts.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.120
As you might already have realized without
some dude analyzing anime on the internet

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:33.750
telling you so, the central theme of fushiguro's
character is that of the shadow.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.969
As we will discuss in a second, this of course
goes for his personality and character arc,

00:03:36.969 --> 00:03:40.469
but it also directly reflects in his actual
jujutsu abilities.

00:03:40.469 --> 00:03:46.609
Megumi is a user of the Ten Shadow Technique,
a rare ability inherited by the powerful Zenin

00:03:46.609 --> 00:03:52.549
family, that allows him to control up to ten
Shikinami, a type of spirit, that can be tamed

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:56.660
and used by a sorcerer.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.640
The real feat of his technique however are
not necessarily the Shikinami himself, though

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:04.300
they are his main source of power, but the
fact that Megumi is able to use shadows as

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.300
a medium.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.849
He is able to summon his creatures directly
from shadows and is even capable of storing

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:11.459
objects or even himself within them.

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:15.260
We actually see him figure this feature of
his technique out in real time in this scene

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:27.120
here. - and 
this is not the only time that its sukuna

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.050
who inspires him to get stronger.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:34.930
I think it's clear that sukuna is not interested
in Megumi for his Shikinami, but for the powers

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:39.650
of his shadows, and so I am sure we will see
fushiguro discover new features and applications

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.770
of this ability in the future.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.080
On top of all this, instead of being too cool
and calculating for getting his hands dirty,

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.960
Megumi actually likes to fight in close combat
together with his shikigami, something else

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:54.060
that gets him respect from Sukuna, as these
sorts of powers are usually used at range

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.010
in the jujutsu world.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:12.039
But unlike his jujutsu where fushiguro is
able to control shadows, in terms of his character,

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:15.980
he carries a deep darkness within himself
that controls him.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.810
And this Shows in a number of ways.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:24.251
One of the first things that immeadietly become
clear when we meet fushiguro, is that just

00:05:24.251 --> 00:05:29.220
like Itadori, he has a weird tendency for
self-sacrifice.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:33.849
we know that fushiguro has a trump card up
his sleeve that even was a threat to sukuna,

00:05:33.849 --> 00:05:36.800
however that card would come at the cost of
fushiguros own life.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.789
And yet the number of times we see him almost
using this last resort in the first season

00:05:41.789 --> 00:05:53.780
of the manga alone is absolutely ridiculous.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:59.210
Pretty much every enemy that manages to get
fushiguro in a bit of a tight spot, he considers

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:04.080
a worthy target to blow himself up with. and
this fact highlight two other negative traits

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.930
of his quite well.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:13.259
The first is, that he lacks self esteem and
is extremely insecure about his own abilities.

00:06:13.259 --> 00:06:18.610
While both gojo and sukuna clearly know that
Megumi is capable of so much more, we are

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:23.990
talking special grade jujutsu here, Megumi
himself, whenever he is challenged, tends

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.830
to just give himself up for the rest.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.870
this makes him different from Yuji, who also
likes to sacrifice himself, but only as a

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:36.960
last resort, after having thrown in everything,
having lost limbs and riddled with wounds.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.350
that is actually the entire point of the baseball
match against the Kyoto students.

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:45.789
The secenes where gojo comments on him and
itadori going for the homerun and Megumi sacrificing

00:06:45.789 --> 00:06:55.330
himself for the team, are pretty straightforward
metaphors for their general mindset.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:07:03.199
The second thing megumis kamikaze attempts
lay open however, go even a bit deeper.

00:07:03.199 --> 00:07:06.540
Not only does he not believe in himself, he
has absolutely no sense of self worth.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:13.400
The underlying reason for this this, is fushiguro's
childhood.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:19.889
When he and his step sister were abandoned
by his father, leaving both of them orphans,

00:07:19.889 --> 00:07:22.370
it left a deep scar on his heart.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:27.509
As a result, and frankly quite understandably,
he has developed severe abandonment issues,

00:07:27.509 --> 00:07:31.000
that make him very cautious about forming
new relationships.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:36.629
And yet, once these relationships are formed,
he would do anything for the people he holds

00:07:36.629 --> 00:07:37.629
dear.

00:07:37.629 --> 00:07:40.690
Gojo plays a very interesting role here.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:45.139
While we know that he technically took Megumi
in and saved him from being sold to the Zenin

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:54.819
family, it doesn't seem like he ever played
the role of a parent for fushiguro.

00:07:54.819 --> 00:07:59.850
The relationship between them is much deeper
than that of teacher and student, but not

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:03.930
deep enough to call it family, at least as
far as we know.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:08.790
And as we see from the small flashback we
get, Gojo, especially in his younger years

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.669
was terrible with people.

00:08:10.669 --> 00:08:16.960
Gojo didn’t really adopt Megumi, he scouted
him as a future potential student.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:21.240
He helped him because he saw that potential
in him to become one of the strong allies

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.240
in the future.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:27.379
His apparent lack of empathy probably just
enforced megumis sene of being worthless.

00:08:27.379 --> 00:08:33.710
Which is tragic, because Gojo clearly cares
for Megumi, but was never able to show it

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:37.050
in a way that gave Megumi self esteem.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:41.120
Instead gojo tries to push Megumi to get better
with the only thing he knows, strength.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:46.050
And so, even though it was a big step for
gojo's character to take him in, it was not

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.490
the best one for Megumi.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:53.750
Interestingly enough however, this has manifested
in probably the best case scenario for Fushiguro.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:59.440
Instead of hating and blaming everyone for
his childhood like sasuke or trying to proof

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:04.940
himself or get attention from others, he has
developed a truly selfless desire to save

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.990
and help those who in his eyes deserve it.

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:10.070
Even at the cost of his own life.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:15.430
In an ironic twist then, while Itadori tries
to be the ultimate selfless person for selfish

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:20.190
reasons, you can check my analysis on him
for more on that, fushiguro due to his lack

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:25.730
of self-worth simply wants to be useful to
others and thus is the truly altruistic one

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:31.750
of the two.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.750
-

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:37.070
This unique dynamic becomes pretty clear in
his encounter with Kamo during the exchange

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.070
event.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:41.130
Kamo claims that both of them are the same.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:42.930
And on the surface that may actually be true.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.160
They are both dark haired, quiet, introverts.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.910
They were both born outsiders.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:49.290
Their parents were both people that the clan
looked down on.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:55.390
The Zenin and Kamo family respectively only
willing To take them in because they were

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:58.330
born with a strong cursed technique.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:04.350
They’re both strategists, who act like they’re
logical, but tend to be swayed by emotions

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.350
instead.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:12.240
They’re both trying to protect someone,
Megumi his sister, and Kamo his mother and

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.240
both only became jujutsu sorcerers to protect
these people.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:17.350
So why does Megumi reject this statement by
Kamo so strictly.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:25.290
After all the poor guy simply wants to be
understood.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:30.770
The reason here is a moral one, that gives
us a lot of insight into Fushiguros character.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:35.779
Kamo basically argues, that as members of
the big clans, they are expected to think

00:10:35.779 --> 00:10:39.770
in terms of what is best for the family and
society as a whole.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:43.890
there is no room to view itadori from a personal
perspective.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:49.030
Sukuna is a threat and thus itadori must be
eliminated for the good of all.

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:55.190
kamo uses this utilitarian argument and his
duty to his family to justify a morally questionable

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:58.670
decision that he personally does not agree
with.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:04.720
To find acceptance within the family and within
the jujutsu world, the rules must be obeyed.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.100
Fushiguro however, despite on the surface
also appearing to be someone who acts rationally

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:13.260
and values rules and laws, actually is a lot
more like his teacher and evaluates decision

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:16.290
of his personal impression and gut feeling.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:21.070
We see this play out pretty nicely in the
very first two episodes, where Megumi even

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:29.240
cites the official jujutsu regulations, threatening
to exorcise itadori.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:36.480
And yet he had already decided all along,
that he wanted to let him live, based on his

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:37.480
personal feelings.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:43.610
And yet, while Kamo's morality is very faulty
at best, Megumi's is based on a wrong assumption

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:44.610
just the same.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:49.250
Similarly to Gon in hunter x hunter, fushiguro
has a very simplified view of human morality.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:53.449
He unconsciously divides people into either
good or bad, black or white, worth saving

00:11:53.449 --> 00:11:58.230
or not worth saving, all based on his personal
impression of them.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.560
Itadori and his sister are good people no
matter what they do.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:05.950
The prisoner Yuji wanted to save, was a bad
guy.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:09.540
And it's not really hard to see, why he thinks
that way.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:17.010
He's a teenager, that was abandoned by both
parents, doesn’t really know how to survive

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:20.951
in the world but he has to pretend that he
does because no one else is there to take

00:12:20.951 --> 00:12:21.951
care of him.

00:12:21.951 --> 00:12:26.120
Add onto that the fact that he was sort of
forced into becoming a jujutsu sorcerer first

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:30.771
by his dad selling him, then by Gojo only
intervening on the premise that he come to

00:12:30.771 --> 00:12:31.771
work with him instead.

00:12:31.771 --> 00:12:32.771
Plus, his inability to help his sister in
her condition.

00:12:32.771 --> 00:12:37.380
And since he actually is an incredibly kind
and caring person at heart, this simplified

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:42.070
way of looking at people helps him protect
himself from people leaving him again.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:47.449
As a result, he tells Itadori, that he might
end up saving people who will kill someone

00:12:47.449 --> 00:12:52.889
in the future.

00:12:52.889 --> 00:12:56.680
The irony of course is that this goes for
fushiguro himself as well.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:13:00.480
Saving Itadori has definitely lead to more
death and suffering and the same might be

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.630
true for other people he sees as good as well.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:09.300
He and Yuji actually have a very similar approach
to the question, what does it mean to live

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.130
a good life worth living.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:13.110
Both think the answer is saving people.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:18.890
However, while Yuji thinks about this in terms
of quantity, saving as many people as possible,

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:24.130
Fushiguro looks at it in terms of quality,
who do I thin is worth saving.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:28.760
And yet, despite this difference in perspective
and despite the apparent Naruto-sasuke dynamic

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:33.870
between them, the relationship between itadori
and fushiguro is not only a major twist on

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:51.550
the shonen trope, but actually the most postive
aspect of the story.

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:55.529
Megumi and Yuji aren't rivals, they are partners.

00:13:55.529 --> 00:13:59.639
They support each other and keep the other
from falling apart under their respective

00:13:59.639 --> 00:14:00.639
darkness.

00:14:00.639 --> 00:14:05.500
Yes, they have contrasting personalities,
and still they are the closest to each other

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:09.680
and understand each other the best, mostly
because they have the same fixation on saving

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:10.680
people.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:15.470
The only argument between them is right at
the start of the story, due to their different

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:19.029
ideas on saving people but then never again.

00:14:19.029 --> 00:14:31.100
And even then, they respect each others moral
views.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:36.390
After itadoris death he even hands the prisoners
name tag to his mother, to honor his friends

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.529
legacy.

00:14:37.529 --> 00:14:42.560
They push each other to grow, without ever
seeing the other person as a threat.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.920
And in direct contrast to the sasukes and
bakugos of the world, instead of refusing

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:50.870
to acknowledge his partner, Fushiguro is the
one that always readily gives validation to

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.769
Itadori and defends him.

00:14:53.769 --> 00:14:56.740
Protecting the other is always a major drive
for both of them alike, whenever they are

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:57.740
together.

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:59.829
The contrast between them, is a sort of ying
and yang, as both of them complete each other

00:14:59.829 --> 00:15:02.600
and are pretty much two sides of the same
coin.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:07.330
In a way their relationship is represented
really nicely, by fushiguros black and white

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:08.670
wolf.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:12.459
Just like Yuji, the white wolf dies during
the cursed womb arc.

00:15:12.459 --> 00:15:18.240
And yet, it's powers and strengths merge with
the black wolf, making him stronger overall.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:23.560
And similarly, Yuji and Megumi increasingly
take on traits from each other as the story

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:24.560
progresses.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:29.950
At the beginning, Megumi is cold, dispassionate,
and entirely selective with his sympathies.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:35.519
Yuji in contrast is warm, friendly, and willing
to sympathize with almost anybody.

00:15:35.519 --> 00:15:41.410
And yet over time, Megumi takes on more of
Yujis emotional, confident and extroverted

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:47.210
self, while Itadori gets a grip on his emotions,
becomes more calculating and is able to make

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:49.060
harder decisions.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:54.079
In a world that has mostly provided nothing
but pain and hardship for them, both make

00:15:54.079 --> 00:16:02.720
each other better and stronger people.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:06.740
And this brings us aaaall the way back to
the initial question.

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:10.360
What happened between these two scenes with
the special curses.

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:15.790
The answer is: Fushiguro has become amore
like Itadori, and finally has the capability

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:25.470
to not only believe in himself, but also be
more emotional and let them become a strength,

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:33.170
- Todo - or as Megumi puts it very thematically
fitting, finally being able to spit out his

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:34.170
shadow.

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:39.240
This unusual rival relationship is one of
the main reasons why jujutsu Kaiser works,

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:44.139
and why it feels so unique and yet familiar
compared to other shounen stories.

00:16:44.139 --> 00:16:48.949
Another really important relationship is that
between Yuji and and the sorcerer who's appeal

00:16:48.949 --> 00:17:00.769
is maybe only topped by Gojo's.

00:17:00.769 --> 00:17:05.440
So I suggest you watch Nanami's video right
here.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.960
Thanks for watching.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:08.810
Peace!

